#: ../../tools/wikipathways_ext_tools.rst 0f463d99e06c436caae3242eaf103195
msgid "WikiPathways_get_pathway_genes tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/wikipathways_ext_tools.rst:64 864a0d4ae6604a578f298cc377486389
msgid "**Name**: ``WikiPathways_get_pathway_genes``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/wikipathways_ext_tools.rst:66 c57fc0fcb81d47049b2510b866d3a6e2
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get all genes (as gene symbols) involved in a "
"WikiPathways pathway. Returns the list of HGNC gene symbols for human "
"pathways, or equivalent organism-specific gene identifiers. Useful for "
"extracting gene sets from curated pathways for enrichment analysis or "
"network building. Example: WP254 (Apoptosis) returns 88 genes including "
"AKT1, APAF1, BAD, BAK1, BAX, BCL2, BCL2L1, BID, CASP3, CASP8, CASP9, "
"CFLAR, CYCS, DIABLO, FADD, FAS, NFKB1, TP53, TRAF1, XIAP, and more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/wikipathways_ext_tools.rst:70 7c98aff681ea4417941d047f86be1816
msgid ""
"``pathway_id`` (string) (required) WikiPathways pathway identifier. "
"Examples: 'WP254' (Apoptosis, 88 genes), 'WP179' (Cell cycle, 100+ "
"genes), 'WP4216' (Chromosomal and microsatellite instability), 'WP1584' "
"(Type II diabetes mellitus)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/wikipathways_ext_tools.rst:73 abd0950d92754db38d59dcb76fb98b2c
msgid ""
"``code`` (string) (optional) Identifier system code for returned genes. "
"Options: 'H' (HGNC symbols, default), 'En' (Ensembl), 'S' (UniProt), 'L' "
"(Entrez Gene), 'Ce' (ChEBI for metabolites)."
msgstr ""

